// The progress table, every row: what each wtc operation guarantees by
// its form, the implementation its object runs and the counts of its
// producers and consumers (WTC/ProgressTable.h, docs/progress.md). The
// table is generated from the code that the passes ask, so this test is
// the place where a change of any row shows. scq, wcq, jiffy and the
// settled rings are the implementations chosen only for a path's
// requirement; wcq is wait-free only where both sides' counts are within
// its 128 thread slots, which the rows at one producer and one consumer
// show.
//
// RUN: wtc-opt %s --wtc-progress-table -o /dev/null | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines

module {}
// CHECK: | operation | impl | np | nc | level | bound | amortised | allocates | kernel | first use | element | reason |
// CHECK-NEXT: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | generic | 1 | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | generic | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | generic | 1 | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | generic | many | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | spsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 8 | - | amortised | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new block when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | spsc_inline | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 8 | - | amortised | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new block when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | mpsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 80 + 64 segment-end pauses | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | mpsc | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | spmc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 6 | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | spmc | 1 | many | wait_free | 6 | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | jiffy | 1 | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when its index is past the last one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push | jiffy | many | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when its index is past the last one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | generic | 1 | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | generic | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | generic | 1 | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | generic | many | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | spsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 5 | - | amortised | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new block when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | spsc_inline | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 5 | - | amortised | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new block when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | mpsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | finite, not instantiated (a run of up to WTC_BATCH_K elements) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | mpsc | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes into a full one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | spmc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 3 | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | spmc | 1 | many | wait_free | 3 | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | none | copy or move constructor | allocates a new segment when the current one is full: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | jiffy | 1 | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when its index is past the last one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | push_deferred | jiffy | many | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | copy or move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when its index is past the last one: the queue is unbounded |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | generic | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | generic | many | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | generic | 1 | many | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | generic | many | many | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | spsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | spsc_inline | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | mpsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | mpsc | many | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | spmc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | spmc | 1 | many | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | jiffy | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_begin | jiffy | many | 1 | wait_free | 0 | - | never | none | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | generic | 1 | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | generic | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | generic | 1 | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | generic | many | many | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | spsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 3 | - | never | futex wake | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | spsc_inline | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 3 | - | never | futex wake | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | mpsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | finite, not instantiated (a run of up to WTC_BATCH_K elements) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | mpsc | many | 1 | lock_free | - | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run into a full one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | spmc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 3 | - | never | futex wake | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | spmc | 1 | many | wait_free | 3 | - | never | futex wake | none | none | - |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | jiffy | 1 | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run past the last one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | batch_end | jiffy | many | 1 | wait_free | not bounded in the counts (the segments it walks to its index's are those linked while it was preempted, not bounded in the counts) | - | once every 1024 | futex wake | per-thread record | move constructor, move-assignment, destructor | allocates a new segment when it publishes the run past the last one |
// CHECK-NEXT: | pop | generic | 1 | 1 | blocking(sf) | - | - | may | none | per-thread record | move constructor, destructor | waits for a push that has taken the cell it reads to fill it, and frees the segments it moves past, and allocates the shared_ptr it returns |
// CHECK-NEXT: | pop | generic | many | 1 | blocking(sf) | - | - | may | none | per-thread record | move constructor, destructor | waits for a push that has taken the cell it reads to fill it, and frees the segments it moves past, and allocates the shared_ptr it returns |
// CHECK-NEXT: | pop | generic | 1 | many | blocking(sf) | - | - | may | none | per-thread record | move constructor, destructor | waits for a push that has taken the cell it reads to fill it, and frees the segments it moves past, and allocates the shared_ptr it returns |
// CHECK-NEXT: | pop | generic | many | many | blocking(sf) | - | - | may | none | per-thread record | move constructor, destructor | waits for a push that has taken the cell it reads to fill it, and frees the segments it moves past, and allocates the shared_ptr it returns |
// CHECK-NEXT: | pop | spsc | 1 | 1 | wait_free | 67 + 96 slip pauses | - | may | none | none | move constructor, destructor | allocates the shared_ptr it returns |
